-- title:
--   Theorem 2.12, p. 8 — amplitude damping and dephasing on one qubit with Hörmander control make the closed class Channel(S) transitive
-- statement:
--   Let $H=\mathbb C^{2^k}$ be the space of $k\ge1$ qubits. Let $S$ be a set of operators with $S=S^*$ that generates a Hörmander system, i.e. the real Lie algebra generated by the anti-Hermitian part of $\operatorname{span}S$ contains $\mathfrak{su}(2^k)$. Suppose $S$ contains the amplitude-damping jump and the dephasing operator on the first qubit:
--   $$|0\rangle\langle1|\otimes I^{\otimes(k-1)}\in S,\qquad Z\otimes I^{\otimes(k-1)}\in S .$$
--   Then the closed class $\overline{\mathrm{Channel}(S)}$ is transitive: for all densities $\rho,\sigma\in\mathcal D(H)$ there is $\Phi\in\overline{\mathrm{Channel}(S)}$ with
--   $$\Phi(\rho)=\sigma .$$
--
--   $\overline{\mathrm{Channel}(S)}$ is the smallest closed set of superoperators that contains $\operatorname{Ad}_{e^{tX}}$ for every anti-Hermitian $X\in\operatorname{span}S$ and $t\ge0$, contains $e^{tL_a}$ for every $a\in S$ and $t\ge0$, where $L_a(\rho)=2a\rho a^*-a^*a\rho-\rho a^*a$, and is closed under composition.
--
--   The theorem says that full unitary control plus two independent jump operators on a single qubit already steer any state of $k$ qubits to any other. A convex hull is not needed (compare Theorem 2.8).
--
--   **Formalization Note** $k\ge1$ is added because the page names the first qubit. The dissipator has the standard sign, against the printed (JU) (see the Setting file). The class is the intersection of all closed sets with (UN), (JU) and (CO), not an arbitrary class with these properties.
-- source:
--   Cai, Govindarajan, Junge, How Far do Lindbladians Go?, arXiv:2504.04883v2, p. 8, Theorem 2.12

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_LindbladReach_MinDiss_Setting

namespace LindbladReach.MinDiss

open scoped Matrix ComplexOrder Matrix.Norms.L2Operator

/-- Theorem 2.12, p. 8: if `S = S*` generates a Hörmander system on `ℂ^{2^k}` and
`|0⟩⟨1| ⊗ I^{⊗(k−1)}`, `Z ⊗ I^{⊗(k−1)} ∈ S`, then the closed class `C̅h̅a̅n̅n̅e̅l̅(̅S̅)̅` is transitive. -/
theorem theorem_2_12 {k : ℕ} (hk : 0 < k) (S : Set (Mat k)) (hS : ∀ a ∈ S, aᴴ ∈ S)
    (hH : IsHormander S) (ha : ampDamp ⟨0, hk⟩ ∈ S) (hz : dephZ ⟨0, hk⟩ ∈ S) :
    IsTransitive (channelClosure S) := by sorry

end LindbladReach.MinDiss
